Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Kazuhiro Ohnishi
Title: Wage-Rise Contract and Mixed Duopoly with Price Competition
Abstract: This paper investigates a mixed duopoly environment in which a private firm competes on price with a public firm. The following timing of actions is considered. In the first stage, each firm non-cooperatively decides whether to adopt a wage-rise contract as a strategic commitment device. If a firm adopts a wage-rise contract, then it chooses an output level and a wage premium rate, and agrees to pay each employee a wage premium uniformly if it actually produces more than the output level. This irreversible behaviour causes changes to the price-competing market environment of the second stage. The paper presents the equilibrium solution of the mixed duopoly model.
Keywords: Mixed market model,price competition,private firm,public firm,strategic commitment
Journal: International Journal of Management, Accounting and Economics
Pages: 898-908
